   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Psychologists use the phrase theory of mind for our ability to imagine what someone else is thinking."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad extends it to a cultural theory of mind: we imagine that other cultures think the way ours does."
    },
    {
     "text": "A secular Westerner may assume that everyone, deep down, values individual freedom, equality between the sexes, and free speech the way she does."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad argues that's a projection. Plenty of people, in plenty of places, sincerely hold very different values."
    }
   ]
