   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "In 2015, Canada's new prime minister, Justin Trudeau, told a magazine that Canada could be the first postnational state, a country with no core identity."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad sees this as cultural empathy taken to its limit. If no culture is better than another, there's nothing in particular to ask newcomers to adopt."
    },
    {
     "text": "Supporters say Canada's openness is a success story. Its immigrants, and especially their children, tend to do well in school and at work."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad replies that success depends on what newcomers believe and whether they integrate, and he points to disputes over public prayer and religious accommodation as warning signs."
    }
   ]
