   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Saad's most serious case is the grooming gang scandal in England."
    },
    {
     "text": "In Rotherham, an independent inquiry led by Professor Alexis Jay estimated that about fourteen hundred children were sexually exploited between 1997 and 2013. Most were girls, some as young as eleven. They were groomed, raped, passed between men and towns, and threatened into silence."
    },
    {
     "text": "Similar networks were uncovered in Rochdale, Telford, Oxford and other towns. In many of these cases, the convicted men were of Pakistani heritage."
    }
   ]
