     "text": "crimes of particular men · condemned by British Muslim leaders",
     "color": "#7bdc8c",
     "d": 1.6,
     "size": 20,
     "in": 3
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The inquiry also found something that shamed the country. Some staff were nervous about identifying the perpetrators' ethnic origins, for fear of being thought racist. Police and social workers often dismissed the girls, or blamed them."
    },
    {
     "text": "A national audit by Louise Casey in 2025 found that the issue had been avoided for years, and that poor record-keeping made it worse."
    },
    {
     "text": "For Saad, this is suicidal empathy at its worst: concern for a community's image outranking the safety of children."
    },
    {
     "text": "It matters to be precise. These crimes were committed by particular men, and British Muslim leaders have condemned them. The scandal is that institutions looked away."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
