      }
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "a1",
     "type": "label",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 160,
     "text": "cultures are not monoliths",
     "color": "#5ec8e5",
     "d": 0.3,
     "in": 1
    },
    {
     "id": "a2",
     "type": "label",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 240,
     "text": "judge practices, not passports",
     "color": "#c792ea",
     "d": 0.6,
     "in": 2
    },
    {
     "id": "a3",
     "type": "label",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 320,
     "text": "the second generation integrates",
     "color": "#7bdc8c",
     "d": 0.4,
     "in": 3
    },
    {
     "id": "a4",
     "type": "label",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 420,
     "text": "name the harm · protect the victims · don’t demonize millions",
     "color": "#ffd166",
     "d": 1.0,
     "size": 20,
     "in": 4
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Critics push back hard here."
    },
    {
     "text": "Cultures aren't monoliths. Every group contains reformers, dissidents, and ordinary people who reject the worst practices, often at great personal risk."
    },
    {
     "text": "Judging a practice is one thing. Suspecting millions of individuals because of where they were born is another, and history shows where that road leads."
    },
    {
     "text": "And in many countries, the children of immigrants end up looking a lot like everyone else, in jobs, values and marriage."
    },
    {
     "text": "Shared ground: you can name a harmful practice, and protect its victims, without demonizing everyone who shares a faith or a passport with its perpetrators. Looking away helps no one."
    }
   ]
  },
